Reuse decision: CHECK. A prior conversation matched, so I confirmed the facts against the corpus rather than relying on it.

```json
{
  "facts": {
    "split": "shlex.split",
    "class": "configparser.ConfigParser"
  }
}
```

- `shlex.split` splits shell-like syntax. `library/subprocess.rst` says `shlex.split` can show how to break a shell command into an argument sequence. `library/whatsnew/3.8.rst` describes `shlex.join` as the inverse of `shlex.split`. The module itself is documented in `library/shlex.rst`.
- `configparser.ConfigParser` reads INI files. `library/configparser.rst` says the module provides the `ConfigParser` class, which implements a basic configuration language similar to Windows INI files. `library/shlex.rst` also describes `configparser` as a parser for files similar to Windows `.ini` files.

Sources: `library/shlex.rst`, `library/subprocess.rst`, `whatsnew/3.8.rst`, `library/configparser.rst`.
